t every  individual weapon leaves totally unique  markings on the ammunition it fires  you've got two cartridge cases of the  microscope left one on the right and I  comparing the fire detail of these well  things say a little bit like a single  bullet barcode fingerprint whatever  analogy you want to use these lines are  all already got pretty oily a  state-of-the-art database allowed  scientists to compare thousands of  samples in just a matter of minutes when  you're searching Laura picked up quite a  number of these links but once you start  getting older shootings the only way  you're ever going to get that sort of  lean is by having an automated system  the team here are investigating dozens  of guns still on the streets boring but  at least the most prolific is now safely  out of the hands of criminals Helen Anne  Smith Sky News
 

